<title>GERMANY: Grundig sees sharply lower loss in 1997.</title>
<headline>Grundig sees sharply lower loss in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's struggling consumer electronics maker Grundig AG said on Thursday it expected to cut operating losses to less than 100 million marks ($59.3 million) this year.</p>
<p>The company earlier reported an operating loss of 382 million marks for 1996, the last year for which its largest shareholder Philips NV must step in to offset losses.  </p>
<p>Grundig sees sharply lower loss =2</p>
<p>Grundig management board chairman Pieter de Jong told a news conference in Nuremberg that achieving this earnings target was &quot;an absolute must&quot;.</p>
<p>He said Grundig planned to cut 1,700 jobs this year, reducing the workforce to 5,000.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 150</p>
